			"Message": "docs(Common): Expand crate architecture Mermaid diagram with subgraphs\n\nRedesign the root README.md Mermaid diagram to reflect the full internal structure of the Common crate rather than a flat overview. The new diagram is organized into three labeled subgraphs:\n\n- Effect System: async traits per service domain, ActionEffect constructors, and their dependency relationship\n- Data Layer: DTO structs and the unified CommonError enum\n- Infrastructure: Transport strategies (gRPC/IPC/WASM with circuit breaker), Telemetry (PostHog + OTLP dual-pipe), and Environment/Effect DI via ApplicationRunTime + Requires/HasEnvironment\n\nConsumer boxes are also expanded: Mountain shows its Environment provider and ApplicationRunTime concrete implementations with arrows back to the abstract traits and effects they fulfill; Air is added as a secondary consumer that uses Transport + Telemetry; Tests are shown mocking traits.\n\nThis gives developers a navigable reference for where new trait definitions, DTOs, transport backends, and telemetry instrumentation fit into the crate's layered architecture.",
			"SHA": "095f64bc847e8abc16057a108becbee0a0f53257"
		},
